"""Pupil-facing copy for the multiple-choice distractor notes (docs/GCSE_MATHS_HINTS.md section 4, Phase 4).

Two tables of new copy, plain string literals so ``models/zorp_voice.py`` can read them with ``ast`` and lint them on
the ``system_hint`` surface (house style, at most two short sentences, at most 120 characters, reading grade, kind
words):

* ``NOTES``       a note id (``mcq.*``) to its text: a slip that mostly multiple-choice questions name.
* ``BANK_NOTES``  a bank note id (``bank.*``) to its text: a slip behind one option of a fixed bank question.

A tagged option stores one note id. It resolves, in this order, in ``BANK_NOTES``, ``NOTES``, then
``misconceptions.MESSAGES`` (so a slip whose line already exists keeps one wording for typed and multiple-choice
answers), then the message of the typed-answer rule of the same id (``misconception_topics.RULES_BY_ID``). The note is
shown beside the pick of that option, so it speaks of "that" answer or says "Check ...".

Rules for every line (same as MESSAGES, section 6 of the plan): it names the slip and the step to fix, never the
correct value or the factor to apply (D5), it hedges, it blames nobody, and it holds no digit.
"""
